The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says "one issue, one fix queued". Its own table says
otherwise. The reports merged into #4471 are three problems, and each needs its own fix. The
queued parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 for all of them when the parser fix ships. Two of the three problems will
still be there. Each problem now has its own ticket, linked below.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} filed={{
  parser: { href: 'https://github.com/angeloocana/support-kb-4471-megadev/issues/1', title: 'issue 1: parser reads dates month first' },
  hint: { href: 'https://github.com/angeloocana/support-kb-4471-megadev/issues/2', title: 'issue 2: booking-v3 date hint' },
  'one-day move': { href: 'https://github.com/angeloocana/support-kb-4471-megadev/issues/3', title: 'issue 3: one-day move' },
}} />

### `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first

Our tenants write the day first, and the shared parser reads every date month first. Day and
month swap: "Booked for 2 December. The invite says 12 February." Every tenant on file has it.
**Fix:** parse dates in the tenant's own locale. This is the fix #4471 queued.

### `hint`: booking-v3 tells people to type the month first

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says,
month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. So the form itself swaps
day and month. Only booking-v3 tenants, and only bookings made through the form. The parser fix
does not touch this code. **Fix:** print the tenant's own date order under the field.

### `one-day move`: the date moves by one day, not by a month

Day and month do not swap here. The booking moves by one day: "Tuesday 6 October showed as
Monday." A client in Lisbon and a client in Toronto got different days for the same meeting.
This points at time-zone handling, not at the parser. The desk already read these reports
differently (`desk-notes.json`), but they stayed filed under `parser`. **Fix:** find where the
booking's date crosses a time zone. The parser fix will not change it.

## Why one ticket hid three

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line. People
  write the same subjects ("Month and day swapped?", "Wrong day on the invite") for different
  bugs, so the subject cannot tell the bugs apart.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The cause depends on the tenant: its
  locale and its booking form. The "tagged as" column below shows how often the two disagree.
- The ticket export repeats some reports across pages. Each report is counted once, by id.

## What #4471 shows

The table from the #4471 page, unchanged. Its `hint` row has no ticket of its own, and the
one-day moves are counted inside `parser`, in the note under it.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do now

- **Engineering:** take the three tickets one by one. Only `parser` is queued.
- **Desk:** merge a new report by its cause (tenant and the way the booking was made), not by
  its subject. A report where the date moves by one day goes to the `one-day move` ticket.
- **Decision 0001:** it is accepted, so nobody edits it. A new decision record should replace
  it with merging by cause.

